          "final_text_tail": "\n\nTemplate path aliasing is implemented in `src/jinja2/loaders.py`:\n\n- **`BaseLoader`** (`src/jinja2/loaders.py:83-124`): `add_alias(alias, target)` (supports overwriting, any string including empty), `remove_alias(alias)` (safe for unknown names), and private `_resolve_template_name()` \u2014 single-step resolution, never recursive. Alias storage is lazily created, so every subclass (including third-party ones without `super().__init__`) gets aliasing for free.\n- **Resolution points**: top of every `get_source` \u2014 `BaseLoader:146`, `FileSystemLoader:247`, `PackageLoader:383`, `DictLoader:465`, `FunctionLoader:509`, `PrefixLoader:553`, `ChoiceLoader:606` \u2014 plus `PrefixLoader.load:569`, `ChoiceLoader.load:621` (the `env.get_template` entry path) and `ModuleLoader.load:694` (which loads via `load`, not `get_source`).\n\nSince resolution happens before the lookup, a broken alias raises `TemplateNotFound` referencing the **target** name, alias names with special characters/`..` never reach path parsing, and loading through an alias returns the real template's source/filename/uptodate.\n\nVerified: all spec scenarios pass (PR example, multiple aliases, no chaining, removal, overwrite, empty/special-char aliases, all 7 loader types incl. composites, `extends` through aliases, uptodate invalidation) and the full existing suite: **841 passed**, no regressions.",
